'' A '-dll' IN --options MAKES A MANIFEST TARGET A DLL, and names its artefact as one (tiko-build
'' B6b): an editor's build configuration passes its flags that way, and [target.tool] says
'' nothing of its kind. It was out/debug/tool.exe holding a DLL.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_MODCACHE=build/.bkf/cache
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' CLEAN: build/.bkf
'' COPY: tests/driver/src/build-pkg => build/.bkf/pkg
'' ARGS: build tool -target win64-msvc --manifest build/.bkf/pkg --options "-dll" --message-format json
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: {"event":"artifact","kind":"dll","path":"build/.bkf/pkg/out/debug/tool.dll"}
'' EXPECT-FILE: build/.bkf/pkg/out/debug/tool.dll
